{
 "config_version": "0.4.3",
 "schema_version": "1.1.0",
 "updated": "2026-08-21",
 "_TAXONOMY_SOURCE": "Concerns, reasons and the seven extraction fields come from the user's operational list. Two levels: CONCERN is what the item is about (Bill Status, Claim Information); REASON is the sub-classification within it. 0.3.0 applied the rules derived from 15 real inbound emails - see SAMPLE_RULES.md and samples.xlsx column M.",
 "_OPEN_QUESTION": "SETTLED 2026-08-19 against 15 real emails: the reasons ARE dispositions, recorded after an agent looks the bill up, and inbound mail states none of them. Reason was blank on 14 of 15 samples; the only one that fired was 'Claim number request', which is the sole reason phrased as a request. Reason output is therefore ADVISORY. Concern and field extraction are the reliable outputs. Re-cutting reasons into things an email can actually say is still open - see SAMPLE_RULES.md Finding 1.",
 "_FIELD_REQUIREDNESS_ASSUMPTION": "RESOLVED 2026-08-19 by the user: on Bill Status, claim_id, date_of_service and expected_amount are REQUIRED - these are the three an agent cannot action a bill without. Everything else stays optional. On Claim Information nothing is required, because that concern is the sender asking to BE GIVEN the claim number; requiring it would flag every such email by definition.",
 "_HOW_TO_ADD_A_CONCERN": [
  "1. Copy a block in 'concerns', give it a new unique 'id' and 'display_name'.",
  "2. Write 3-5 'prototypes': plain-English sentences describing what the sender wants.",
  "   These are embedded and compared semantically. Descriptions, not keywords.",
  "3. Add 'examples': short realistic phrasings (identifiers faked, never real PHI).",
  "4. Add 'keyword_rules.positive' phrases that are strong giveaways.",
  "5. List 'fields'. Reference a regex by 'pattern_ref' - never write regex here.",
  "   Set 'require_label': true whenever the pattern is shared with another field.",
  "6. Optionally add 'reasons' for sub-classification, same prototype/keyword shape.",
  "7. Run: python -m email_triage check-config",
  "NOTE: confidence is shrunk when a concern has fewer than 4 prototypes+examples,",
  "so a thin concern always routes to review until fleshed out (pipeline SP-1.1-20)."
 ],
